    "q-288069": {
      "dom_id": "step-q288069",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $2x-3=2x+4$\n\nII. $-5x+7=-2x-2$\n\nIII. $4x+1=4x+1$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =2x+4 \\\\ 2x-3-2x & =2x+4-2x \\\\ -3 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x-3=2x+4$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+7 & =-2x-2 \\\\ -5x+7+2x-7 & =-2x-2+2x-7 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-5x+7=-2x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =4x+1 \\\\ 4x+1-4x & =4x+1-4x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-288069-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-288069-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only",
